WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.880
[soft suspenseful music]

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.200
♪

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.600
- When I was a kid.

4
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.840
every adult I knew
shared one thing in common...

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.120
A gap in their lives when
everything appeared uncertain

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.760
and time itself
seemed to stand still.

7
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.000
When they talked about it.

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.960
they simply called it
"the war."

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.720
For six dark years.
the world was on fire.

10
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.280
Cities were demolished

11
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.920
and whole populations
threatened.

12
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.600
When would the war end?
No one knew.

13
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.880
How would it end?
No one knew.

14
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.800
Life was in stasis.

15
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.040
The war is now a part
of our culture.

16
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.280
portrayed in movies
and on television

17
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.280
and novels and history books.

18
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.000
The Allies usually defeat
the enemy

19
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.560
and save the world.

20
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.280
But the grim reality of the war

21
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.960
is almost impossible
to comprehend.

22
00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.320
Over 65 million people
are killed...

23
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.440
The majority civilians.

24
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.840
Everyone fought some version
of the war.

25
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.840
beginning with the mothers
and fathers

26
00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.000
who sent their children overseas

27
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.120
not knowing when or if they
would ever see them again.

28
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.360
And. of course.
the soldiers. sailors.

29
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.200
airmen. and marines...
Often just a bunch of kids...

30
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.600
Who served with honor
and bravery

31
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:25.280
to liberate enslaved peoples
and preserve human dignity.

32
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.280
In doing so. they saved
that which is most precious

33
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.920
and valued by us all...

34
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.640
Freedom.

35
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.360
The Second World War

36
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.920
is the largest event
in human history.

37
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.680
No part of the globe
is unaffected.

38
00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:44.680
World War II changed everything
for all of us.

39
00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.160
[dramatic music]

40
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.720
- All wars change the world.

41
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.680
but none of them
changed the world

42
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.600
like the Second World War did.

43
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.600
- Japan's on the march.
Germany's on the march.

44
00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.000
- No one can imagine

45
00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.800
the nightmare
they're about to unleash...

46
00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.680
The most destructive war
in human history.

47
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.360
- Suddenly the world
is turned upside down.

48
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.840
and all hell is let loose.

49
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.160
♪

50
00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.680
- The West is stunned
by the speed of the advance.

51
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.640
- You get the Allies.
led by the big three...

52
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.200
Roosevelt. Churchill. Stalin...

53
00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.080
Men who are dealing

54
00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.280
with immensely complicated
questions.

55
00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.440
- It's the biggest military
operation of human history.

56
00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.856
- The Allies have to come
together.

57
00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.280
not just militarily.

58
00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.696
but industrial scale

59
00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.520
it's a global perspective.

60
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.560
- They have to fight
in every climate.

61
00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.240
from the Arctic
to the jungles of the Pacific

62
00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.400
to the deserts of Africa
and the depths of the ocean.

63
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.280
♪

64
00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.160
- But there was
no certainty of victory.

65
00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:55.600
It was going to be
a horrific bloodbath.

66
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.600
- We see humans
at their absolute worst.

67
00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.120
how they treat
other human beings.

68
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.720
And we see them
at their absolute best.

69
00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.120
willing to give their lives
that others might live.

70
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.200
- World War II was a struggle
in which there could be

71
00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.640
one victor and one vanquished.

72
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.296
♪

73
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.920
[explosions.
air raid sirens wailing]

74
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.280
♪

75
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:33.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

76
00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.720
[distant bells tolling]

77
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.800
♪

78
00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.840
- Sometimes
the most monumental events

79
00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.680
begin without fanfare...

80
00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.360
before the world wakes.

81
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.440
♪

82
00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.560
And so it is

83
00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.880
on the 1st of September. 1939.

84
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.120
as dawn breaks over a sleeping
city on the Baltic Sea.

85
00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.240
that the bloodiest conflict
in all history begins.

86
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:15.960
♪

87
00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.800
[gunfire]

88
00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.800
♪

89
00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.000
- This is the national program
from London.

90
00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.240
Germany has invaded Poland.

91
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.840
- Heavy outbreaks of fighting

92
00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.640
along the German-Polish
frontier.

93
00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.600
- [speaking German]

94
00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:41.960
♪

95
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.400
- [speaking German]

96
00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.160
♪

97
00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.760
[air raid sirens wailing]

98
00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.200
[people shouting]

99
00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.920
♪

100
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.920
- In just a matter of hours.
a million and a half men...

101
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.360
1.300 planes...

102
00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.800
and 2.750 tanks

103
00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.160
crossed the Polish border
at lightning speed.

104
00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.320
♪

105
00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.520
- September 1. 1939...

106
00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.000
A storm breaks over Poland.

107
00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.520
♪

108
00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.720
- The Germans are racing
through with tanks

109
00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:42.760
and with artillery.
following up with the infantry

110
00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.880
and accompanied
by the Luftwaffe.

111
00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.360
[bombs whistling]

112
00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.160
♪

113
00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.960
And all of a sudden.
people were waking up

114
00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.560
to the sound of tanks rumbling
through the town

115
00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.960
not really knowing
what was happening.

116
00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.840
- You're going to see
waves of trucks

117
00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.480
and mechanized
and motorized vehicles.

118
00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.320
It looks a bit like
a science-fiction novel.

119
00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.720
like all those novels written
in the '20s and '30s

120
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.000
about what the war
of the future would look like.

121
00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.200
And. suddenly. in 1939.
the future is now.

122
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.080
[tense orchestral music]

123
00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:19.680
♪

124
00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.600
- At 11:00 a.m..

125
00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.320
Hitler arrives
at a Berlin opera house

126
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.040
where he's gathered
the Reichstag.

127
00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.240
[crowd cheering]

128
00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.520
♪

129
00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:45.680
♪

130
00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.720
- This is the moment Hitler's
been waiting for all his life.

131
00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.200
He's been the leader
of the Nazi party since 1921.

132
00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.760
He comes to power in '33.
He rearms the country in '35.

133
00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:02.480
And since then. it's been
prepare. prepare. prepare.

134
00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.240
But Hitler wants a war.

135
00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.160
[cheers and applause]

136
00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.040
- The invasion follows
months of diplomatic tension

137
00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.440
over a strip of land known
as the Polish Corridor...

138
00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.920
Land that had once
been part of Germany...

139
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.520
but was ceded to Poland
to give her access to the sea

140
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.640
after the First World War.

141
00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.160
♪

142
00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.720
20 years earlier.
global leaders gathered

143
00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.480
in the French city of Versailles

144
00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.360
to sign the historic treaty
ending that war.

145
00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.960
After four years
of brutal fighting.

146
00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.400
an alliance led
by Britain and France

147
00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.160
and supported
by the United States

148
00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.800
emerged victorious.

149
00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.040
♪

150
00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.400
Germany. its military exhausted

151
00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.920
and its people near
starvation. had lost.

152
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.200
And now they would pay
the price of defeat.

153
00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.840
- The Treaty of Versailles

154
00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.480
takes territories
away from Germany.

155
00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.560
It strips Germany of
populations and raw materials.

156
00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.920
It turns the entire
German merchant marine

157
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.240
over to the Allies.

158
00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:19.200
It imposes reparations
on the Germans.

159
00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.240
- The Allies
were attempting to limit

160
00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.520
the future power of Germany.

161
00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.280
The effects of the
First World War were so grave.

162
00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.520
they were so catastrophic

163
00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.800
that no one wanted
to see a repeat of that.

164
00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.880
- One young Austrian corporal
fighting for the German army

165
00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.160
is Adolf Hitler.

166
00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:41.440
Like many. he is shocked
by the way the war ends.

167
00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.360
- Your average German
was surprised by the news

168
00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.640
of the armistice because
it happened so suddenly.

169
00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.240
The army was still in the field.

170
00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.400
and there was the sense
that we haven't been invaded

171
00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.240
and thoroughly beaten.

172
00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:54.040
- It was personally
a tragedy for Hitler.

173
00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:55.840
He heard the news
of the armistice

174
00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.760
when he was still ill from
injuries sustained in battle.

175
00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:03.760
He did not process
the end of the war well.

176
00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:07.360
He did not accept
the defeat of Germany.

177
00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.640
- Surviving soldiers
come home angry

178
00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.800
and confused.

179
00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.880
- Frankly. the response
of many of them

180
00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.200
is disillusionment.

181
00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.760
Four years at the front.

182
00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.600
I managed to dodge
all those bullets.

183
00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.040
and now I came home
and this is what I fought for?

184
00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.400
[suspenseful music]

185
00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:26.000
- When Hitler comes
back from the war.

186
00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.640
he learns to talk
to former soldiers

187
00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.120
who are now disgruntled
and begins to feel the fact

188
00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.240
that he's actually
quite a good speaker.

189
00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:36.240
- [speaking German]

190
00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.920
[people cheering]

191
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.840
- He attends a meeting
of a small group

192
00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:41.160
which will become

193
00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.240
the National Socialist
German Workers.

194
00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.160
or Nazi Party.

195
00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.680
He finds something attractive.

196
00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.040
This is a party of grievance

197
00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.160
talking about how Germany
could be transformed

198
00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.160
and Germany could be made
powerful again.

199
00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.040
In 1921. Hitler's talent
for public speaking

200
00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.320
makes him the leader
of this tiny party.

201
00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.680
- Hitler's first move
is an attempted coup

202
00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.360
against the Bavarian
state government in Munich.

203
00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.920
♪

204
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.160
But it fails.
and he's arrested for treason.

205
00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.560
♪

206
00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:12.840
At his trial.
the judge allows Hitler

207
00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.880
to publicly share
his movement's grievances

208
00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:20.760
against war guilt.
reparations. and communism.

209
00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.760
In jail.
he publishes his memoir.

210
00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.760
"Mein Kampf."
or "My Struggle."

211
00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:28.760
♪

212
00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:32.760
With Hitler's notoriety.
Nazi Party membership grows

213
00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.960
as Germany's Weimar Republic

214
00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.320
moves through the unstable '20s.

215
00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.560
The economy is burdened
by heavy war reparations.

216
00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:46.560
In 1923.
the cost of one loaf of bread

217
00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.200
rockets from 3 marks
to 80 billion.

218
00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.520
♪

219
00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:55.920
The years that follow
are unstable. chaotic.

220
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.520
♪

221
00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.120
Hitler's Nazi Party
fuels racial hatred

222
00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:04.240
against Jews
and fears about communism.

223
00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.520
Then. just as the economy
is recovering.

224
00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:12.400
the Great Depression throws
6 million Germans out of work.

225
00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:16.240
- People in Germany are
confused. bewildered. unhappy.

226
00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.920
And so there's a real opening

227
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.056
for a leader who will speak
all these lines perfectly

228
00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:21.936
and talk about. how I'm going
to bring the Germans

229
00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.400
back together.

230
00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:28.160
- In the 1932 elections.
Germany is deeply divided.

231
00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.160
♪

232
00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.960
But President von Hindenburg.

233
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.360
backed by conservative
businessmen.

234
00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:37.000
appoints Hitler chancellor
to run the government

235
00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.360
at the beginning of 1933.

236
00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:42.000
♪

237
00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:44.640
- In 1934. Hitler declares

238
00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:47.520
that he will now continue
to be chancellor

239
00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.840
and take over the role
of the president as well.

240
00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:54.040
He's transformed what was
a democracy in Germany

241
00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:58.720
into a one-party
and a one-man dictatorship.

242
00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.160
He's become the German leader.
the Fuehrer.

243
00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.360
♪

244
00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:08.160
- His first promise as Fuehrer
is to reclaim the land

245
00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.400
Germany lost at Versailles.

246
00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.320
He seizes the Rhineland.

247
00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:14.720
Austria. and the Sudetenland...

248
00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.200
German-speaking parts
of Czechoslovakia.

249
00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:20.720
By 1938. just four years later.

250
00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.920
he's reshaped the map of Europe.

251
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.600
Desperate to avoid another war.

252
00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:30.840
Britain and France allow
Hitler to expand his empire.

253
00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.720
- In 1938 at Munich.

254
00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.760
Neville Chamberlain.
the British Prime Minister.

255
00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:39.280
and the French actually made
a deal with Hitler.

256
00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.280
What he wanted was the
Sudetenland of Czechoslovakia.

257
00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.880
The British had said. fine.

258
00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.600
we'll just dismantle an entire
country to keep you happy.

259
00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.760
- But when Hitler
turns to Poland.

260
00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:53.240
the West finally takes a stand.

261
00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:58.360
The Poles have already endured
centuries of foreign rule.

262
00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:00.360
The country regains
its independence

263
00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.040
as part
of the Versailles Treaty.

264
00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.880
But its new borders now
include 20.000 square miles

265
00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.360
of what had been German land.

266
00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.960
♪

267
00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:15.400
In summer 1939.
the British and the French

268
00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.920
sign a guarantee with the Poles

269
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.360
promising military assistance
if the Germans invade.

270
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.400
♪

271
00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.640
- Hitler. speaking
to his officers...

272
00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.040
They're asking him questions.

273
00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.936
Well. what is the attitude
of the West gonna be

274
00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:31.120
if you attack Poland?

275
00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.800
And he snorted.
Don't worry. he said.

276
00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.040
I've seen my opponents
at Munich.

277
00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.680
They're little worms.

278
00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.400
- Hitler doesn't believe

279
00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:41.360
the West has the will
to go to war.

280
00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:42.760
♪

281
00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.480
So he moves across the border.

282
00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:48.440
ready to invade
with the full force

283
00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.160
of the Nazi Wehrmacht.

284
00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.240
♪

285
00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.056
[tense music]

286
00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.360
♪

287
00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.400
- In the first 24 hours
of the invasion...

288
00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.120
♪

289
00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:05.360
The Germans take out railroads.

290
00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.720
bridges. and airfields.

291
00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:10.720
♪

292
00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.760
The destruction paves the way

293
00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:16.160
for their army to advance
deep into Poland.

294
00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.880
♪

295
00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.960
- The Poles have a modern army.

296
00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.320
It's the fifth-largest army
in the world.

297
00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.000
♪

298
00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.440
And it's equipped
with modern tanks.

299
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:32.560
with all sorts of artillery
and armored trains.

300
00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.800
But Hitler has been putting
almost all his resources

301
00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.440
into equipping the military.

302
00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.920
The Poles were outgunned
by the Germans.

303
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.320
who had three-to-one tanks
and five-to-one airplanes.

304
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.680
So there's no question that the
Germans were a superior force.

305
00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.240
♪

306
00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.800
- Despite those odds.

307
00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:54.560
the Poles are determined
to defend their country.

308
00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:57.320
♪

309
00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.760
- Everyone had to help.

310
00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.440
and soldiers conscripted
civilians on the street.

311
00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:03.160
putting them to work.

312
00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:05.840
I saw one man who was stopped
six times on his way home

313
00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.520
with a loaf of bread.

314
00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:10.960
♪

315
00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:14.160
- The Poles remain resilient.

316
00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.280
♪

317
00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.120
But the question is.

318
00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:21.200
what will Britain and France do?

319
00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:23.240
- Here. as ever
in critical days.

320
00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:26.760
has seen the coming and going
of the leaders of the country.

321
00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:30.320
- The British and French had
an alliance with the Poles.

322
00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.000
They have to defend Poland.

323
00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:35.040
But they're not
militarily prepared to do so.

324
00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.320
and they're not
mentally prepared to do so.

325
00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.720
The home fronts
in Britain and France

326
00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.760
are dead set against war.

327
00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.080
- British Prime Minister
Neville Chamberlain

328
00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.560
tells Parliament
he's considering

329
00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.480
issuing an ultimatum.

330
00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.320
But many feel he's backtracking

331
00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:52.800
on his promise to Poland.

332
00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.400
♪

333
00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:58.360
- This is a profound injury
to British honor.

334
00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.400
that if we don't act
and declare war.

335
00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.320
no other country will ever trust

336
00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.200
a treaty with Britain
ever again.

337
00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:08.080
- Britain delivers
an ultimatum to Berlin

338
00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:11.360
on the morning
of September 3. 1939.

339
00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.640
♪

340
00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:17.360
Hitler has until 11:00 a.m.
to withdraw his forces.

341
00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:19.480
♪

342
00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.640
[bell tolls]

343
00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:22.160
It's ignored.

344
00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.960
[bell tolling]

345
00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.160
- This morning.

346
00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.720
the British ambassador in Berlin

347
00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:31.320
handed the German government
a final note.

348
00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:33.600
And. consequently.

349
00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:38.400
this country is at war
with Germany.

350
00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.840
[air raid sirens wailing]

351
00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.280
- In cities across Britain.

352
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.360
air raid sirens
signal a strange new era.

353
00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:50.480
and millions of gas masks
are sent to British homes.

354
00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:54.360
♪

355
00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:55.960
Across the Atlantic.

356
00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:59.520
America is just emerging
from the Great Depression

357
00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:01.920
and not prepared for war.

358
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.640
♪

359
00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.760
The peacetime army is small.

360
00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:07.360
♪

361
00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.280
And neutrality laws

362
00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.760
make it nearly impossible
to aid the Allies.

363
00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.720
♪

364
00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.560
In the White House.
the press gathers for one

365
00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:20.440
of President Roosevelt's
fireside chats.

366
00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.480
- I have said.
not once but many times.

367
00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.040
that I have seen war

368
00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.840
and that I hate war.

369
00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:32.040
I say that again and again.

370
00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:35.600
I hope the United States
will keep out of this.

371
00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:40.240
And I give you assurance
and reassurance

372
00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.600
that every effort
of your government

373
00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:45.600
will be directed
toward that end.

374
00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:48.280
- Most Americans.
when they're asked.

375
00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.880
should the United States
get involved?

376
00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:54.360
90% of Americans say
absolutely not.

377
00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.360
But Franklin Delano Roosevelt.

378
00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:01.440
he's watching what's happening
in Europe very closely.

379
00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:05.080
The question is about freedom
and democracy.

380
00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.160
He understands what is at stake.

381
00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.760
♪

382
00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.280
- In Germany.
Hitler is surprised

383
00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.760
when Britain and France
declare war.

384
00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.400
- When the British declaration
of war is made.

385
00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:18.160
Hitler receives it in silence.

386
00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.040
And for a couple of moments.

387
00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.880
he stares at his
foreign minister. Ribbentrop.

388
00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:26.400
And then with a quite
vicious tone to his voice.

389
00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.600
he says. what now?

390
00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:31.400
[tense music]

391
00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.960
♪

392
00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:37.640
- Despite the British
and French declaration.

393
00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.640
Hitler continues
his master plan for Poland

394
00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.160
and sends in the Luftwaffe.

395
00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.480
♪

396
00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:49.640
Hitler's air force
is led by a trusted member

397
00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:51.840
of his inner circle...

398
00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:54.200
Field Marshal Hermann Goering.

399
00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.200
♪

400
00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.360
- Goering's a German celebrity.

401
00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:00.920
World War I. he was the head
of the Flying Circus.

402
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.920
the Fliegender Zirkus. this
elite group of fighter pilots.

403
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.280
♪

404
00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.440
And so he's well-known
in Germany.

405
00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:10.760
He's very handsome.
very charismatic guy.

406
00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.400
But there's also
a very dark side to Goering.

407
00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.440
He feels deeply embittered
by the way the war ended.

408
00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:19.200
and he falls
under Hitler's spell.

409
00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:23.040
And he's able to get
huge appropriations from Hitler

410
00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:24.760
for Luftwaffe procurement.

411
00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.080
♪

412
00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.560
- Goering's elite pilots
are young

413
00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.880
and have spent thousands
of hours in training.

414
00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.680
♪

415
00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.960
From the cockpits of heavy
bombers. they drop explosives.

416
00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.920
♪

417
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.280
But it's
the precision dive bombers

418
00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.040
that wreak the most terror.

419
00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.080
♪

420
00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.520
- The Sturzkampfflugzeug.

421
00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.640
the Stuka
as it's usually abbreviated...

422
00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.520
You know. it's not
a particularly swift craft.

423
00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.800
But they dive at an almost
90-degree angle...

424
00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.840
♪

425
00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.120
And literally drop a bomb
in your lap.

426
00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:02.600
♪

427
00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:05.760
And there's even a bit
of psywar here as well.

428
00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:09.480
As they're coming down on you.
there's a siren screaming.

429
00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.680
[Stuka siren wailing]

430
00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:16.920
- In Poland. there are pilots
flying at low altitude

431
00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.400
who can see women and children
fleeing the roads

432
00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.960
who actually target them
deliberately.

433
00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:26.160
[Stuka siren wailing]

434
00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:29.080
[somber music]

435
00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.480
♪

436
00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:33.400
Polish civilians
experience modern war

437
00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:36.360
in an unbelievably
horrifying way.

438
00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:41.960
♪

439
00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:43.560
They see people killed.

440
00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.680
They see bodies all around them.

441
00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:47.760
It's a nightmare.

442
00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.840
♪

443
00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.160
- Poland is being destroyed.

444
00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:57.040
♪

445
00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:58.960
It is not clear when

446
00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:03.160
or even if Britain and France
can send forces to help.

447
00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.640
♪

448
00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:09.736
[tense music]

449
00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.080
♪

450
00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.080
- On day three...

451
00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.880
Adolf Hitler boards his
heavily armored private train.

452
00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.240
the "Amerika."

453
00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:19.600
♪

454
00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.680
He named it after his admiration

455
00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:25.400
for the way America
settled a vast continent.

456
00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:27.800
Now traveling towards Poland.

457
00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:31.840
he looks out on the territory
he needs to conquer...

458
00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:35.320
Land stretching deep
into Eastern Europe.

459
00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:40.040
Lebensraum. living space
for his new German empire.

460
00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.400
♪

461
00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:44.840
This is his
and Germany's destiny.

462
00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:47.400
- Hitler talks about
a thousand-year Reich.

463
00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:50.320
Its borders would stretch
from the Atlantic in the west

464
00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:51.760
to Scandinavia in the north

465
00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:53.600
and the Mediterranean
in the south.

466
00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:55.400
Poland and the lands to the east

467
00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.320
play a special role in
Hitler's foreign-policy plans.

468
00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:00.200
They're wide-open spaces.

469
00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:03.800
farmland as far
as the eye could see.

470
00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:07.200
- In order to achieve
this vast empire.

471
00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:10.120
Germans must clear out
the people living there

472
00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:12.360
in a remorseless race war.

473
00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:14.200
♪

474
00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:17.080
- Adolf Hitler's whole worldview

475
00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:20.520
is based on a kind
of neo-Darwinism

476
00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:25.240
in which every single act
is a biological struggle.

477
00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:28.120
warfare between different races.

478
00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:31.040
♪

479
00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.680
He believes that
the Aryan race. the Germans.

480
00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:36.120
is the superior race
on the planet.

481
00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:39.640
It's destined to rule Europe
and indeed the world.

482
00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:41.160
♪

483
00:22:41.240 --> 00:22:43.240
- Until now.
Hitler's main target

484
00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:47.160
has been
Germany's Jewish population.

485
00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:50.800
Under his orders. they lost
their status as citizens.

486
00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:53.280
had their wealth
and property seized.

487
00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:56.040
and many were forced into exile.

488
00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:58.280
- Hitler believes
that humanity is locked

489
00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.120
in this existential battle

490
00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:03.560
between Aryans. as he
describes them. and Jews.

491
00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:05.960
And Jews are
supposedly responsible

492
00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:10.080
for all of society's
and the world's ills.

493
00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:11.400
- So who is responsible

494
00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:13.960
for the German loss
in World War I?

495
00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:15.520
Jewish people.

496
00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:18.960
Who is responsible
for economic inequality?

497
00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.520
Jewish people.

498
00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:23.000
They control media. newspapers.

499
00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.600
all the businesses.

500
00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:25.920
The reason you are poor

501
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:27.800
is because
they are hoarding money.

502
00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:30.040
- What the Nazis are seeking
to do at this stage

503
00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:31.880
is to make life so unpleasant.

504
00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:34.600
so difficult for Jewish people
within the Reich

505
00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:36.600
that they want to leave.

506
00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:41.120
- Hitler also wants to remove
the Slavs of Eastern Europe.

507
00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:44.440
including the people of Poland.

508
00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:49.720
♪

509
00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:51.040
Day four...

510
00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:53.400
Hitler reaches
the Polish front lines.

511
00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:57.000
where he holds a photo
opportunity with his troops.

512
00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:59.440
- He makes himself very visible.

513
00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:01.920
goes to the front.
and he's greeted

514
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.960
by these thousands
and thousands of people.

515
00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:05.760
They're all vying
with one another

516
00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:08.200
to get close to Adolf Hitler.

517
00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:11.880
- He's fought in World War I.
He's a battle-tested leader.

518
00:24:11.960 --> 00:24:15.160
He's taken back
historic German territory.

519
00:24:15.240 --> 00:24:16.840
He's built the armed forces.

520
00:24:16.920 --> 00:24:18.320
They listen to him.

521
00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:21.800
♪

522
00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:23.920
- These German soldiers
marching on Poland

523
00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:27.120
believe in Germany's destiny...

524
00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:31.000
that they will be the creators
of the great new Germany.

525
00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:33.520
- This is the first action
they've had militarily

526
00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:36.920
since the Black Day
of the German Army in 1918.

527
00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.320
And it is an average infantryman

528
00:24:39.400 --> 00:24:42.040
from the First World War
who's leading it.

529
00:24:42.120 --> 00:24:43.360
♪

530
00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:45.720
So this is redemption

531
00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:50.240
20 years after what never
should have happened happened.

532
00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:52.720
♪

533
00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:54.560
- Shadowing his invading forces

534
00:24:54.640 --> 00:24:57.040
is another wing
of the Nazi regime...

535
00:24:57.120 --> 00:24:58.440
♪

536
00:24:58.520 --> 00:25:00.840
The Protection Squadron...

537
00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:05.520
In German.
the Schutzstaffel. or SS.

538
00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:07.720
They were Hitler's
personal bodyguards

539
00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:10.240
as he rose to power.

540
00:25:10.320 --> 00:25:13.080
But under the leadership
of Heinrich Himmler.

541
00:25:13.160 --> 00:25:15.320
they become
a paramilitary outfit

542
00:25:15.400 --> 00:25:18.360
at the heart of the regime.

543
00:25:18.440 --> 00:25:20.720
- Himmler is somebody

544
00:25:20.800 --> 00:25:23.440
who has a sadistic streak.

545
00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.176
He's quite meek. he's not
particularly assuming.

546
00:25:25.200 --> 00:25:27.200
he's certainly not
very physically impressive.

547
00:25:27.280 --> 00:25:29.520
but he's somebody who's got
a burning desire

548
00:25:29.600 --> 00:25:30.760
to achieve things.

549
00:25:30.840 --> 00:25:33.640
He gets drawn
into the Nazi loop.

550
00:25:33.720 --> 00:25:35.120
and then over a period of time.

551
00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:37.720
he eventually takes control
of the SS.

552
00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:39.400
- Himmler has developed the SS

553
00:25:39.480 --> 00:25:42.120
from a small
kind of a bodyguard unit

554
00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:44.080
that's supposed
to really protect Hitler...

555
00:25:44.160 --> 00:25:45.360
♪

556
00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:48.440
Into a vast militarized force.

557
00:25:48.520 --> 00:25:49.800
♪

558
00:25:49.880 --> 00:25:52.560
- In Poland.
the SS units fan out

559
00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:55.200
across the newly
occupied territory.

560
00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:58.920
as does a special wing
of the SS...

561
00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.520
The Einsatzgruppen...

562
00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:03.840
mobile death squads.

563
00:26:03.920 --> 00:26:04.920
♪

564
00:26:08.720 --> 00:26:10.176
[tense music]

565
00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:12.000
♪

566
00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:17.080
- In September 1939.
during the invasion of Poland.

567
00:26:17.160 --> 00:26:18.520
the Nazi Einsatzgruppen

568
00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:21.840
are under orders
to neutralize any opposition.

569
00:26:21.920 --> 00:26:23.600
♪

570
00:26:23.680 --> 00:26:26.800
- The Einsatzgruppen
are specifically set up

571
00:26:26.880 --> 00:26:29.800
to go into towns. villages.

572
00:26:29.880 --> 00:26:31.720
and other areas of Poland

573
00:26:31.800 --> 00:26:33.640
to kill civilians.

574
00:26:33.720 --> 00:26:35.520
That's their only job.

575
00:26:35.600 --> 00:26:38.800
Professors. landowners.
politicians.

576
00:26:38.880 --> 00:26:40.720
newspaper editors.
these sorts of people...

577
00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:43.200
They were targeted and killed
because these were the people

578
00:26:43.280 --> 00:26:45.440
who are identified
as possibly leading

579
00:26:45.520 --> 00:26:48.240
some sort of resistance
against the German forces.

580
00:26:48.320 --> 00:26:51.720
And this is something that the
Poles could not have known yet

581
00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:53.640
on those first days
of the invasion.

582
00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:56.280
that this wasn't just going
to be a military invasion.

583
00:26:56.360 --> 00:27:00.040
but this was also going to be
a war of annihilation.

584
00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:02.600
♪

585
00:27:02.680 --> 00:27:06.720
- For Hitler. this is a chance
not just to destroy Poland

586
00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:08.600
but to clear Poland.

587
00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:11.600
to crush the Polish people.
who are Slavs.

588
00:27:11.680 --> 00:27:13.520
And Slavs in the Nazi ideology

589
00:27:13.600 --> 00:27:16.040
are Untermenschen.
"underhumans."

590
00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:18.920
But it's more than that.
There are also Jews in Poland.

591
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.360
♪

592
00:27:20.440 --> 00:27:22.400
- For centuries.
Poland has been home

593
00:27:22.480 --> 00:27:24.760
to millions of Europe's Jews.

594
00:27:24.840 --> 00:27:28.120
who fled there to avoid
religious persecution.

595
00:27:28.200 --> 00:27:30.040
- The Jews
originally settled there

596
00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:33.400
because it was
the freest kingdom in Europe.

597
00:27:33.480 --> 00:27:35.320
Now they found themselves

598
00:27:35.400 --> 00:27:38.800
in a terrifying. murderous trap.

599
00:27:38.880 --> 00:27:42.400
- The SS drag Orthodox Jewish
men out into the streets.

600
00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:45.720
and they desecrate
their clothes and their hair.

601
00:27:45.800 --> 00:27:47.920
They smash up synagogues.

602
00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:50.600
They are seeking
to amplify the terror

603
00:27:50.680 --> 00:27:52.880
that they've sought
to develop within the Reich

604
00:27:52.960 --> 00:27:54.840
towards Jews within Poland.

605
00:27:54.920 --> 00:27:56.440
♪

606
00:27:56.520 --> 00:27:58.200
- These acts of brutality

607
00:27:58.280 --> 00:28:00.560
escalate into public executions.

608
00:28:00.640 --> 00:28:02.920
[tense somber music]

609
00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:06.080
In the town of Konskie
on September 12th.

610
00:28:06.160 --> 00:28:10.240
German troops order local Jews
to the town square...

611
00:28:10.320 --> 00:28:13.040
to dig the grave
of a German soldier.

612
00:28:13.120 --> 00:28:16.320
♪

613
00:28:16.400 --> 00:28:21.040
- This rather humiliating
forced grave-digging exercise

614
00:28:21.120 --> 00:28:23.640
quickly descends into a pogrom.

615
00:28:23.720 --> 00:28:24.880
♪

616
00:28:24.960 --> 00:28:26.280
Jews are shot.

617
00:28:26.360 --> 00:28:28.440
You know. they try
and run away from the scene.

618
00:28:28.520 --> 00:28:29.960
They're quickly apprehended.

619
00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:31.520
♪

620
00:28:31.600 --> 00:28:35.240
And in total. 22 Jews
are killed on that day.

621
00:28:35.320 --> 00:28:36.600
♪

622
00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:38.680
This was happening
across Poland...

623
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:40.400
♪

624
00:28:40.480 --> 00:28:44.240
The brutal mass murder
of innocent civilians.

625
00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:50.120
♪

626
00:28:50.200 --> 00:28:52.480
- Nine days into the invasion.

627
00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:56.160
Britain and France continue
to mobilize their forces.

628
00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:58.880
Civilians are being killed
in the streets.

629
00:28:58.960 --> 00:29:00.640
but the army isn't defeated.

630
00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:04.400
With their capital city.
Warsaw. now the target.

631
00:29:04.480 --> 00:29:07.160
two Polish armies
stage a counterattack

632
00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:08.920
to the west of the city.

633
00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:11.440
Polish cavalry
and reconnaissance tanks

634
00:29:11.520 --> 00:29:14.840
drive German forces back
12 1/2 miles

635
00:29:14.920 --> 00:29:17.080
in the Battle
of the Bzura River.

636
00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:19.160
- You know. all too often.
the Polish campaign

637
00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:21.120
is talked about
as some kind of pushover.

638
00:29:21.200 --> 00:29:23.080
But the Poles fought hard.

639
00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:24.840
- The classic stereotype
of the Poles

640
00:29:24.920 --> 00:29:27.480
is that they're all on their
horses with sabers drawn.

641
00:29:27.560 --> 00:29:30.120
riding toward tanks who
are just shooting them down.

642
00:29:30.200 --> 00:29:31.280
This is absurd.

643
00:29:31.360 --> 00:29:33.360
The Poles were
very sophisticated.

644
00:29:33.440 --> 00:29:37.960
- Very finely trained soldiers.
extremely brave.

645
00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:39.960
♪

646
00:29:40.040 --> 00:29:43.800
- As Poles fight
under German bombardment...

647
00:29:43.880 --> 00:29:45.920
Prime Minister
Neville Chamberlain

648
00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:48.840
and French Premier
Edouard Daladier meet

649
00:29:48.920 --> 00:29:51.120
for a supreme war council

650
00:29:51.200 --> 00:29:54.320
and reach a grave decision.

651
00:29:54.400 --> 00:29:55.880
- Daladier and Chamberlain

652
00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:58.800
agree to leave Poland
to its fate.

653
00:29:58.880 --> 00:30:00.520
They also adopt formally

654
00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:02.680
what they call
the long war strategy...

655
00:30:02.760 --> 00:30:05.440
The idea that they have
superior resources to Germany

656
00:30:05.520 --> 00:30:08.520
and that. over time. those
resources will come to bear

657
00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:10.240
in the Allies' favor.

658
00:30:10.320 --> 00:30:12.480
- Although the statement
that is given

659
00:30:12.560 --> 00:30:15.840
to the world's press is one
of wholehearted support.

660
00:30:15.920 --> 00:30:19.760
Poland is essentially cast
to the four winds.

661
00:30:19.840 --> 00:30:22.200
- There is
one British politician

662
00:30:22.280 --> 00:30:25.520
who has always wanted to take
a more aggressive position

663
00:30:25.600 --> 00:30:27.400
against the Nazis.

664
00:30:27.480 --> 00:30:29.520
Appointed to the new war cabinet

665
00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:32.800
is Hitler's most vocal critic
in the West...

666
00:30:32.880 --> 00:30:36.440
First Lord of the Admiralty
Winston Churchill.

667
00:30:36.520 --> 00:30:38.080
♪

668
00:30:38.160 --> 00:30:41.400
- Throughout the 1930s.
Churchill had spoken up

669
00:30:41.480 --> 00:30:43.400
with concern
about German rearmament.

670
00:30:43.480 --> 00:30:46.080
about the failure
to take effective measures

671
00:30:46.160 --> 00:30:48.800
to enforce
the Versailles Treaty.

672
00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:52.200
It's clear now that Germany
couldn't be trusted

673
00:30:52.280 --> 00:30:54.040
as a diplomatic partner.

674
00:30:54.120 --> 00:31:01.000
♪

675
00:31:01.080 --> 00:31:03.440
- Two weeks into the invasion...

676
00:31:03.520 --> 00:31:06.200
♪

677
00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:07.880
The Poles seem abandoned.

678
00:31:07.960 --> 00:31:10.440
and their counteroffensive
is collapsing.

679
00:31:10.520 --> 00:31:12.320
♪

680
00:31:12.400 --> 00:31:17.240
The German 3rd. 8th. and 10th
armies encircle Warsaw.

681
00:31:17.320 --> 00:31:22.000
♪

682
00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:24.680
The capital is a city
of palaces.

683
00:31:24.760 --> 00:31:27.120
churches. and opera houses...

684
00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:30.600
The heart of the Polish nation.

685
00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:33.960
But now Warsaw is in ruins

686
00:31:34.040 --> 00:31:35.640
and under siege.

687
00:31:35.720 --> 00:31:41.000
♪

688
00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:43.000
- Bombs were falling.
and everybody

689
00:31:43.080 --> 00:31:45.760
was trying to help get people
out of the rubble.

690
00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:46.920
When your roof is burning.

691
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:48.760
when your children
are in hospital

692
00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:50.040
because they've been bombed...

693
00:31:50.120 --> 00:31:52.080
I mean. these are
shocking moments.

694
00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:55.400
- American photographer
and cameraman Julien Bryan

695
00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:57.200
is in Poland's capital

696
00:31:57.280 --> 00:31:59.480
filming suffering and defiance.

697
00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:00.960
♪

698
00:32:01.040 --> 00:32:03.600
He pleads for Poland.

699
00:32:03.680 --> 00:32:07.160
- President Roosevelt
and the people of America.

700
00:32:07.240 --> 00:32:08.840
listen to my story.

701
00:32:08.920 --> 00:32:10.200
♪

702
00:32:10.280 --> 00:32:13.960
America must act.
It must help.

703
00:32:14.040 --> 00:32:15.560
- As help is called for.

704
00:32:15.640 --> 00:32:18.320
there is an army preparing
to sweep in.

705
00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:19.880
♪

706
00:32:19.960 --> 00:32:22.720
They're not coming
from the west...

707
00:32:22.800 --> 00:32:24.360
but from the east.

708
00:32:24.440 --> 00:32:26.360
♪

709
00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:32.736
[tense music]

710
00:32:32.760 --> 00:32:34.280
♪

711
00:32:34.360 --> 00:32:35.920
- On the 17th of September.

712
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.960
Joseph Stalin
calls the German ambassador

713
00:32:39.040 --> 00:32:41.160
to the Kremlin and says.

714
00:32:41.240 --> 00:32:43.080
we're going to invade
Eastern Poland.

715
00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:48.520
♪

716
00:32:48.600 --> 00:32:51.880
- Poland's fate isn't sealed
just by the Nazis.

717
00:32:51.960 --> 00:32:54.040
The communists of Soviet Russia

718
00:32:54.120 --> 00:32:56.080
also sense opportunity.

719
00:32:56.160 --> 00:33:00.320
And so does
their all-powerful master.

720
00:33:00.400 --> 00:33:03.560
- Stalin is one of the most
extraordinary figures

721
00:33:03.640 --> 00:33:06.680
in the history
of the 20th century.

722
00:33:06.760 --> 00:33:10.280
From the very beginning of the
Russian Revolution in 1917.

723
00:33:10.360 --> 00:33:12.320
he's been part
of the tiny clique

724
00:33:12.400 --> 00:33:15.160
that's been running Russia
and has emerged

725
00:33:15.240 --> 00:33:19.160
as the dominant leader
of the whole Soviet Union.

726
00:33:19.240 --> 00:33:21.800
The inner circle called him
[speaks Russian]...

727
00:33:21.880 --> 00:33:23.520
The master. the boss.

728
00:33:23.600 --> 00:33:25.640
But in public.
he was the [speaks Russian]...

729
00:33:25.720 --> 00:33:27.280
The leader.

730
00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:28.560
But he was a tough man.

731
00:33:28.640 --> 00:33:31.360
a morbid man. a mysterious man.

732
00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:35.280
- He learned the hard way
in the Russian Civil War

733
00:33:35.360 --> 00:33:37.640
that you operate ruthlessly.

734
00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:39.800
You sacrifice. you attack.

735
00:33:39.880 --> 00:33:42.720
you show no quarter
to your enemies.

736
00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:46.120
Stalin saw the world
in geopolitical terms.

737
00:33:46.200 --> 00:33:48.240
He recognized
that the Soviet Union

738
00:33:48.320 --> 00:33:52.320
couldn't survive isolated.
surrounded by adversaries.

739
00:33:52.400 --> 00:33:56.480
- He had to play the poker game
of diplomacy and war.

740
00:33:56.560 --> 00:33:59.240
And the players were
the Western democracies.

741
00:33:59.320 --> 00:34:03.000
led by England and France.
and the dictatorships.

742
00:34:03.080 --> 00:34:06.160
His great fear was that
the two sides would gang up

743
00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:09.600
against him
and destroy the Soviet Union.

744
00:34:09.680 --> 00:34:13.040
And all of his decisions
came from this fear.

745
00:34:13.120 --> 00:34:15.480
- In August 1939.

746
00:34:15.560 --> 00:34:19.080
just one week
before Germany invades Poland.

747
00:34:19.160 --> 00:34:21.640
Joseph Stalin shocked the world

748
00:34:21.720 --> 00:34:25.560
when he signed a nonaggression
pact with Adolf Hitler.

749
00:34:25.640 --> 00:34:28.800
- The revelation
of the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact

750
00:34:28.880 --> 00:34:31.640
causes mayhem
in the Western capitals.

751
00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:34.680
It changes everything.
It's a complete shock.

752
00:34:34.760 --> 00:34:36.000
♪

753
00:34:36.080 --> 00:34:37.760
For the last sort of five years.

754
00:34:37.840 --> 00:34:39.240
the two dictatorships...

755
00:34:39.320 --> 00:34:42.040
Nazi Germany
and Stalinist Russia...

756
00:34:42.120 --> 00:34:45.920
Had been pouring excrement
over each other in the media.

757
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.080
They had been calling each
other every name under the sun.

758
00:34:49.160 --> 00:34:53.840
And for each. the other was
the quintessential enemy

759
00:34:53.920 --> 00:34:56.040
of everything they believed.

760
00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:58.680
And now. suddenly.
there's a thawing.

761
00:34:58.760 --> 00:35:00.640
and the next thing you know.

762
00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:03.200
Ribbentrop is flying to Moscow.

763
00:35:03.280 --> 00:35:05.040
♪

764
00:35:05.120 --> 00:35:08.800
- In August 1939.
by signing a pact with Hitler.

765
00:35:08.880 --> 00:35:10.200
Stalin helps to ensure

766
00:35:10.280 --> 00:35:12.400
that the Second World War
will break out.

767
00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:14.880
In fact. it makes it
virtually a certainty

768
00:35:14.960 --> 00:35:16.360
that such a war will break out.

769
00:35:16.440 --> 00:35:17.600
♪

770
00:35:17.680 --> 00:35:19.400
- The pact promises

771
00:35:19.480 --> 00:35:23.240
a decade of nonaggression
between the two regimes.

772
00:35:23.320 --> 00:35:26.000
But there's
another secret protocol

773
00:35:26.080 --> 00:35:28.240
which carves up Eastern Europe.

774
00:35:28.320 --> 00:35:30.840
sharing the land between them.

775
00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:33.120
First up is Poland.

776
00:35:33.200 --> 00:35:34.480
♪

777
00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:36.880
- Neither the Germans
nor the Soviets

778
00:35:36.960 --> 00:35:39.280
wanted Poland to exist.

779
00:35:39.360 --> 00:35:41.640
They both saw it as an affront.

780
00:35:41.720 --> 00:35:43.080
Poland had historically been

781
00:35:43.160 --> 00:35:44.680
a province
of the Russian Empire.

782
00:35:44.760 --> 00:35:47.080
and the Soviets want that back
as a buffer

783
00:35:47.160 --> 00:35:50.800
against this stronger Germany
that's emerging.

784
00:35:50.880 --> 00:35:53.880
- The division of Polish
territory favored the Soviets.

785
00:35:53.960 --> 00:35:57.560
who got more territory
than the Germans did.

786
00:35:57.640 --> 00:36:01.040
So it's actually the Soviet
invasion of Eastern Poland

787
00:36:01.120 --> 00:36:03.880
that decides the fate of Poland.

788
00:36:03.960 --> 00:36:11.080
♪

789
00:36:11.880 --> 00:36:15.560
- The Red Army pours into
Poland's eastern provinces.

790
00:36:15.640 --> 00:36:16.840
♪

791
00:36:16.920 --> 00:36:18.680
They. too. carry orders

792
00:36:18.760 --> 00:36:22.880
to eradicate Polish leaders
and culture.

793
00:36:22.960 --> 00:36:25.880
- When the Red Army
goes into Eastern Poland.

794
00:36:25.960 --> 00:36:29.960
they are accompanied inevitably
by the secret police. the NKVD.

795
00:36:30.040 --> 00:36:32.760
and they arrest
all these people...

796
00:36:32.840 --> 00:36:37.360
Writers. diplomats.
aristocrats. army officers.

797
00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:39.160
Some of them
are killed instantly.

798
00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:40.720
Some of them are deported.

799
00:36:40.800 --> 00:36:44.600
And a large number of them.
between 20.000 and 30.000.

800
00:36:44.680 --> 00:36:49.320
are stowed in camps
near the Katyn woods.

801
00:36:49.400 --> 00:36:53.040
All of these people are
to be secretly executed.

802
00:36:53.120 --> 00:36:54.720
shot in the back of the head.

803
00:36:54.800 --> 00:36:57.760
[somber music]

804
00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:00.000
[wind whistling softly]

805
00:37:00.080 --> 00:37:04.960
- On September 22. 1939.
in the town of Brest-Litovsk.

806
00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:08.800
Nazi and Soviet generals
gather to watch a parade

807
00:37:08.880 --> 00:37:10.840
of both armies.

808
00:37:10.920 --> 00:37:13.640
[tense music]

809
00:37:13.720 --> 00:37:16.720
- There's this free mingling
of German and Soviet forces.

810
00:37:16.800 --> 00:37:18.600
The two sides
are sort of mixing.

811
00:37:18.680 --> 00:37:20.440
sharing cigarettes.
sharing anecdotes.

812
00:37:20.520 --> 00:37:23.720
And they even develop
almost a slang between them.

813
00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:26.760
[speaks Russian]
"Together strong."

814
00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:28.360
♪

815
00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:30.160
- If you're a Polish person.

816
00:37:30.240 --> 00:37:34.360
to see these two people that
have always been dangerous

817
00:37:34.440 --> 00:37:36.840
on both sides of you

818
00:37:36.920 --> 00:37:41.720
working together to see that
Poland once again disappears.

819
00:37:41.800 --> 00:37:44.000
you had to feel like
there's no help close by.

820
00:37:44.080 --> 00:37:45.600
♪

821
00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:49.160
- As Poland burns
and her enemies celebrate...

822
00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:50.640
♪

823
00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:52.560
One city resists...

824
00:37:52.640 --> 00:37:53.960
♪

825
00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:55.160
Warsaw.

826
00:37:55.240 --> 00:37:56.320
♪

827
00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:01.416
[tense music]

828
00:38:01.440 --> 00:38:02.120
♪

829
00:38:02.200 --> 00:38:03.600
[distant explosions]

830
00:38:03.680 --> 00:38:05.360
- Despite weeks of assault.

831
00:38:05.440 --> 00:38:08.160
Warsaw has not yet surrendered.

832
00:38:08.240 --> 00:38:11.400
Surviving Polish troops
rush to the capital.

833
00:38:11.480 --> 00:38:15.640
where 300.000 soldiers
and civilians hold the city.

834
00:38:15.720 --> 00:38:17.240
♪

835
00:38:17.320 --> 00:38:19.000
To break the resistance.

836
00:38:19.080 --> 00:38:22.360
Goering orders the largest
air raid ever seen.

837
00:38:22.440 --> 00:38:24.920
♪

838
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:28.080
[air raid sirens wailing.
people shouting]

839
00:38:28.160 --> 00:38:30.320
♪

840
00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:32.560
[bombs whistling]

841
00:38:32.640 --> 00:38:36.080
♪

842
00:38:36.160 --> 00:38:37.680
- Goering levels Warsaw

843
00:38:37.760 --> 00:38:39.760
with no regard
for civilian casualties.

844
00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:42.040
They strew thousands of pounds
of high explosive

845
00:38:42.120 --> 00:38:45.640
and incendiary bombs.
firebombs over Warsaw.

846
00:38:45.720 --> 00:38:47.840
And they reduce it to rubble.

847
00:38:47.920 --> 00:38:50.760
[fires crackling]

848
00:38:50.840 --> 00:38:53.680
[somber music]

849
00:38:53.760 --> 00:38:57.320
♪

850
00:38:57.400 --> 00:38:59.720
- It is the largest
incendiary bombing

851
00:38:59.800 --> 00:39:02.400
that the world has ever seen.

852
00:39:02.480 --> 00:39:04.840
Air raids last
for the entirety of the day.

853
00:39:04.920 --> 00:39:06.600
People are trapped
in their basements.

854
00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:09.360
they're trapped in courtyards.
they're trapped in stairwells.

855
00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:11.920
Those who crawl out when
the bombardment is over...

856
00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:14.760
There's no water.
there's nothing to feed them.

857
00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:18.680
♪

858
00:39:18.760 --> 00:39:21.840
- 20% of the city is destroyed
in one way or another.

859
00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:24.320
And about 18.000 people
are injured or killed

860
00:39:24.400 --> 00:39:26.000
in these bombardments.

861
00:39:26.080 --> 00:39:29.600
- And the city finally
has to surrender.

862
00:39:29.680 --> 00:39:31.760
♪

863
00:39:31.840 --> 00:39:35.040
- [speaking Polish]

864
00:39:45.840 --> 00:39:53.120
♪

865
00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:58.960
- In London. Winston Churchill
warns his country

866
00:39:59.040 --> 00:40:01.720
that this is just the beginning.

867
00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:06.080
- Poland has been overrun
by two of the great powers

868
00:40:06.160 --> 00:40:10.040
which held her in bondage
for 150 years

869
00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:13.240
but were unable to quench
the spirit

870
00:40:13.320 --> 00:40:15.840
of the Polish nation.

871
00:40:15.920 --> 00:40:18.640
The heroic defense of Warsaw

872
00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:21.840
shows that the soul of Poland

873
00:40:21.920 --> 00:40:23.760
is indestructible.

874
00:40:23.840 --> 00:40:26.160
♪

875
00:40:26.240 --> 00:40:29.560
The British Empire
and the French Republic

876
00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:32.560
have been at war
with Nazi Germany

877
00:40:32.640 --> 00:40:34.640
for a month tonight.

878
00:40:34.720 --> 00:40:36.360
♪

879
00:40:36.440 --> 00:40:39.200
Directions have been given
by the government

880
00:40:39.280 --> 00:40:43.160
to prepare for a war
of at least three years.

881
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:47.120
♪

882
00:40:47.200 --> 00:40:50.960
- But Churchill has received
a signal of hope.

883
00:40:51.040 --> 00:40:52.640
A few weeks earlier.

884
00:40:52.720 --> 00:40:55.920
President Roosevelt sent him
a note congratulating him

885
00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:58.120
on his new role
in the war cabinet

886
00:40:58.200 --> 00:41:02.360
and opening up a secret line
of communication.

887
00:41:02.440 --> 00:41:06.440
- Once Germany invades Poland.
Roosevelt infers that this war

888
00:41:06.520 --> 00:41:09.560
is going to be sizable
in its scope

889
00:41:09.640 --> 00:41:11.080
and that the United States

890
00:41:11.160 --> 00:41:14.120
is probably going to need
to intervene at some point.

891
00:41:14.200 --> 00:41:18.600
Churchill has this reputation
of being a fighter.

892
00:41:18.680 --> 00:41:22.040
It's really telling
that Roosevelt seeks him out

893
00:41:22.120 --> 00:41:25.240
rather than Chamberlain
at this critical juncture

894
00:41:25.320 --> 00:41:27.560
at the beginning
of the Second World War.

895
00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:30.160
- So there's this relationship
that develops

896
00:41:30.240 --> 00:41:32.640
between
Franklin Delano Roosevelt

897
00:41:32.720 --> 00:41:34.320
and Winston Churchill.

898
00:41:34.400 --> 00:41:36.520
There's an understanding
on the part of Roosevelt

899
00:41:36.600 --> 00:41:39.280
that there is someone
in the leadership

900
00:41:39.360 --> 00:41:42.440
of Great Britain
who understands what's at stake

901
00:41:42.520 --> 00:41:46.120
and just how dangerous
this moment is.

902
00:41:46.200 --> 00:41:47.840
♪

903
00:41:47.920 --> 00:41:51.720
It's not simply about
the German invasion of Poland.

904
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:53.280
♪

905
00:41:53.360 --> 00:41:55.920
They're two men who are united

906
00:41:56.000 --> 00:41:59.000
in their belief
that Adolf Hitler

907
00:41:59.080 --> 00:42:01.920
is perhaps the most dangerous
man on the planet.

908
00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:03.080
♪

909
00:42:03.160 --> 00:42:04.520
- After the surrender.

910
00:42:04.600 --> 00:42:07.880
Hitler travels to Warsaw
to survey the ruins.

911
00:42:07.960 --> 00:42:09.560
♪

912
00:42:09.640 --> 00:42:11.720
He points
at the utter destruction

913
00:42:11.800 --> 00:42:15.200
and tells the officers
who are with him...

914
00:42:15.280 --> 00:42:18.000
this is the real meaning of war.

915
00:42:18.080 --> 00:42:21.600
♪

916
00:42:21.680 --> 00:42:24.880
In less than a month.
a major European nation

917
00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:27.000
has been removed from the map.

918
00:42:27.080 --> 00:42:31.520
It will be engulfed in darkness
for most of the next six years.

919
00:42:31.600 --> 00:42:36.320
And it's only the beginning.
as Hitler looks to the West.

919
